course: dictionary
lesson: 10061
title: Tetanus and words from health lessons
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Words from health and science lessons often have clues close by. «Tetanus is caused by a germ in soil and dirt, not by rust; a deep cut from any dirty object can let it in, and vaccination protects you.» The clues are germ, soil, cut and vaccination, so tetanus must be an illness that a germ causes.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you guess. The sentence says the germ lives in soil and dirt, not in rust. If you guessed that rust causes tetanus, the sentence corrects you. Then test your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: Some words explain themselves in brackets or next to a harder word. A jab is an everyday word for an injection. Put the two together and a tetanus jab is an injection that protects you from tetanus. When you are not sure, ask an adult or check a dictionary.
fact: Tetanus is a serious illness caused by germs that live in soil and dust.
fact: The germs get into the body through a cut or wound, and they make muscles stiff and tight, especially in the jaw.
fact: «Lockjaw» is an old name for tetanus.
fact: A tetanus jab is an injection, also called a vaccine, that protects you from this illness.
fact: Deep cuts from dirty or rusty objects should be cleaned well, and an adult should check whether you need a tetanus jab.
exercise: «Tetanus is caused by a germ in soil and dirt, not by rust.» What causes tetanus? | Rust on old nails | Sunshine and cold weather | *Germs that live in soil and dust | Eating too many sweets
exercise: After a deep cut from a rusty nail, what should you do? | Wait until it turns black | *Clean it well and tell an adult | Put a bandage on it and forget it | Hide it from your family
exercise: Which illness is another name for lockjaw? | *Tetanus | Chickenpox | Asthma | Measles
test: Tetanus makes muscles stiff and tight, especially where? | The ears | The knees | The fingers | *The jaw
test: What is a tetanus jab? | A cut that needs a plaster | A kind of rust | *An injection that protects you from tetanus | A type of soil
exam: Why does the sentence «Tetanus germs live in soil, so the danger in a wound is the dirt, not the rust.» tell you that dirt matters most? | It says germs live only in water | It says dirt is safe and rust is dangerous | It says rust is safe to touch | *Because the germs live in soil, so the dirt in a wound is the danger
